{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short; git diff -- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; git log -1 --oneline; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794403932000-engineer-cc3-fix-r7.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":" M src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n?? CC3-REVIEW-R7.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794374077000-engineer-cc3-fix-r2.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794376197000-engineer-cc3-fix-r3.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-engineer-cc3-fix-r4.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794394490000-engineer-cc3-fix-r6.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794403932000-engineer-cc3-fix-r7.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\nindex 69e2f344..f31f24e3 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n@@ -1482,15 +1482,35 @@\n         ;; nothing (absence, never invention).\n         handles (volatile! {})\n         retaining-load (fn [vm packet]\n-                         (when-let [admission\n-                                    (get (:call-site-round-claims state)\n-                                         (first packet))]\n-                           (when-let [retained\n-                                      (retain-packet-call-provenance!\n-                                        state packet admission)]\n-                             (vswap! handles assoc\n-                                     [admission (first packet)]\n-                                     (:handle retained))))\n+                         ;; r7: retention is a side artifact outside\n+                         ;; every manifest hash; its failure (a store\n+                         ;; refusing the write, a provenance refusal)\n+                         ;; must never change the round's observable\n+                         ;; behavior — the value, the indexer's own\n+                         ;; publication Warning, or the error text.\n+                         ;; At master (no retention on this path) a\n+                         ;; broken store still evaluated the program\n+                         ;; and reported the failure through the\n+                         ;; indexer; a throwing materialize here turned\n+                         ;; that round into `Error: …` and lost the\n+                         ;; value.  Failure-isolate retention: on any\n+                         ;; throw, retain nothing for this packet\n+                         ;; (absence, never invention) and load as\n+                         ;; before.\n+                         (try\n+                           (when-let [admission\n+                                      (get (:call-site-round-claims state)\n+                                           (first packet))]\n+                             (when-let [retained\n+                                        (retain-packet-call-provenance!\n+                                          state packet admission)]\n+                               (vswap! handles assoc\n+                                       [admission (first packet)]\n+                                       (:handle retained))))\n+                           (catch #?(:cljd Object\n+                                     :clj Exception\n+                                     :cljs :default) _\n+                             nil))\n                          (load-program vm packet))\n         {:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n         (try (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n0ec036d1 feat(yang.clojure): cc3 — lowering provenance and oracle C1 occurrence-key bridge\n# cc3 fix round r7 — findings (muse-wonder-1.0)\n\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance`, base HEAD `0ec036d1`. Nothing committed. One file changed: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` (uncommitted). (Mirror of the requested deliverable path, which is outside this worktree's writable root.)\n\n## Item 1 — the 6 round-text failures: FIXED\n\n**Mechanism (named).** cc3 r2 item 4 connected provenance retention to the production load path: `run-evaluator-stage` in `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` wraps every loader with `retaining-load`, which — before calling the real `load-program` — calls `retain-packet-call-provenance!`, which calls `jing/materialize!` twice on the session's `:index-store`. Ordinary Clojure rounds do create a claim (verified by probe: evaluating `(defn g …)` then `(g 10)` populates `repl/call-provenance-handles`), so on a store whose `put-bytes-fn` throws, `materialize!` threw *inside the loader*, before the program ever ran. `run-evaluator-stage` propagated it, `eval-program`'s catch routed it to `consume-failed-round`, and the round rendered `Error: store refused the write` with the value (`3`, `5`) lost and the query path's `(:yin.repl.query/index-unavailable)` refusal never produced. At master there is no retention on this path: the program evaluates, and the publication failure is reported by the indexer's own stage as the trailing `Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (materialize failed: …)`. The regression window is r2's wrapper (retention connection), made unconditional-on-claim in the r4–r6 rounds; cc3's diff does not touch `index.cljc`/`query.cljc`, confirming the wrapper as the sole suspect.\n\n**Fix.** Failure-isolate retention inside `retaining-load`: the claim lookup + `retain-packet-call-provenance!` now run in a `try` catching `#?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default)`; on any throw, nothing is retained for that packet (absence, never invention — no handle is recorded) and `(load-program vm packet)` proceeds exactly as at master. Retention is a side artifact outside every manifest hash, so its failure must not change the round's value, Warning, or error text. No test was re-pinned; the provenance functionality (side artifacts, admission pairing, coverage refusals) is untouched, and `yang.clojure-callsite-test` (36/403, including the durable/survives-failure/survives-link-resume retention tests) stays green, proving retention still persists on the success path.\n\n**Red-first evidence.** Before the fix, laptop at `0ec036d1`: `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test` → 45 tests / 593 assertions / **6 failures** (`index_test.cljc:560`, `:563`; `query_test.cljc:390` ×4), with actual text `Error: store refused the write\\nWarning: …` vs expected `3\\nWarning: …` / `(:yin.repl.query/index-unavailable)`. After the fix: **0 failures**.\n\n## Item 2 — cross-node corpus hang: NOT REPRODUCED LOCALLY; no in-process path found; deferred to Shiva\n\n**What I checked.** `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test/corpus-jvm-serves-node-decodes-over-cbor` runs two processes: a Node test process and a JVM child (`java -cp <test-classpath> clojure.main -m dao.stream.ws-project-peer --serve`). I verified directly that the JVM peer loads **zero** `yin.*` namespaces (`java -cp … clojure.main -e \"(require 'dao.stream.ws-project-peer) … (loaded-libs)\"` → no `yin` libs), and the Node side of that test (`node-dialer`, `read-reflection-corpus`, `project/dial-step!` ticker) requires only `dao.stream.*` — neither side ever calls `yin.repl`'s loaders, `run-evaluator-stage`, or the retention wrapper. cc3's diff touches no `dao.stream`, `dao.jing`, or derive-consumer on this path (corpus values cross via `dao.jing.stream/wrap-payload`, whose inputs cc3 does not change). So the prompt's hypothesis — wrapper materialization blocking the served read in-process — has no code path on this test; the only couplings are host-level (shadow compile time, parallel-lane CPU contention on Shiva starving the 20 s `settle-ms` window, CBOR being the largest/slowest corpus).\n\n**Wrapper cost, measured (JVM, laptop).** Threaded-state probe, 30 rounds of `(g 10)` after `(defn g [x] (+ (* x 2) (- x 1)))`: with the default index store 1368 ms, with `:index-store nil` (retention no-ops) 1175 ms → retention adds ≈6 ms/round (~16%) on the JVM. That is the entire load-path delta vs master besides the r3 error-path `ex-info` wrap; it cannot block a read it never runs in. I made no async redesign (bounds forbid redesigning the approved provenance functionality, and there is no evidence the wrapper is on this path).\n\n**Local run attempt.** `bb` is unavailable on this laptop (confirmed: no `bb` on PATH; node v26.1.0, clojure, java 17 present). The direct substitute — `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:ns-regexp \"dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test\"}'` — fails before compiling: \"SHADOW-CLJS FAILED TO LOAD … Syntax error macroexpanding at (shadow/cljs/util.clj:1:1)\" (no `node_modules` in this worktree; shadow 3.3.5 cannot load). Per the prompt's own fallback, the cross-node laptop run is **deferred to Shiva**, where the re-run of `bb test:sub:cljs dao.stream` must prove it. The CLJ standing net below was run with `-n dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test` as instructed; that namespace is CLJS-only, so the JVM runner silently ran the other four namespaces (124 tests) and did not exercise it — recorded here as unverified locally, not as green.\n\n## Item 3 — coverage gap closed (standing net)\n\n`yin.repl.index-test` and `yin.repl.query-test` are now in the round's verification net (they caught this regression class; index-test had never been in the laptop net). The cross-node test joins the net at Shiva via `bb test:sub:cljs dao.stream`.\n\n## Verification table (laptop, after fix)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test` (red-first, before fix) | 45/593, **6 failures** |\n| Same, after fix | 45/593, **0 failures** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test` | 124 tests / 993 assertions, **0 failures** (cross-node ns is CLJS-only, not exercised on JVM) |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 36/403, **0 failures** |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| Cross-node corpus (Node lane) | **Unverified locally** — `bb` absent, shadow-cljs fails to load; deferred to Shiva re-run |\n\n## Change summary\n\n- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` (`run-evaluator-stage`'s `retaining-load`): retention attempt wrapped in a failure-isolating `try/catch`; on throw, retain nothing and load normally. No other file changed. Nothing committed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
